WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.835
The war in Ukraine has drastically

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:04.104
raised the alert level for NATO's forces

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.339
operating in Eastern Europe.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.273
CNN's Jim Sciutto

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.174
got an exclusive

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.043
look at how the alliance is training

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.478
for the possibility

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:15.181
of being attacked by the Russians.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.584
Dizzying speed.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.118
The fighter

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.818
jets zoom

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.488
low over the NATO's task force again

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.391
and again and again.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.560
These are Polish and German Air Force

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.095
jets, but they're playing the role

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.764
of Russian aircraft

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.765
on attack,

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.432
part of air

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.600
defense exercises

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.968
in what sailors and commanders

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.771
say is an increasingly tense environment

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.107
on NATO's Eastern Front.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.710
Flying, sailing, readying

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.179
for any and all combat scenarios.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.082
These exercises are taking place

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.150
in the Baltic Sea

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.984
within striking

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.585
distance of the Russian enclave

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.720
of Kaliningrad.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.821
And it's no accident

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.557
that NATO's pilots are flying MiG 29

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.093
and Sukhoi 24 aircraft,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.162
just like the Russians fly

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.296
its German frigate

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.065
Mecklenburgh for Permission

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.599
is the flagship of NATO's

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.801
very high readiness

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.803
task force designation.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.870
The task force commanding

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.206
officer says they take seriously.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.341
We are training exercising right now,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.443
but when it's required,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.645
we can relate to every mission,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.914
from maritime security operations

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.282
to deterrence

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.017
to defend the alliance

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.051
whenever this is required

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.753
in a very short moment.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.655
The task force is now approaching

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.857
Russian territory, Kaliningrad.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.325
And so we're practicing

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.927
heightened awareness

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.195
that means greater awareness

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:35.895
of everything

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.998
from cyber attacks to close observation

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.401
or even harassment by Russian aircraft

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.103
and warships.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:43.770
Yankee

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.972
raising awareness of Russian forces

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.240
is high

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.007
right in the middle

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.676
of the simulated attack.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.545
Officers on deck report Russian aircraft.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.413
Actual

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.481
Russian Sukhoi

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.516
fighter jets approaching fast.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.918
Sailors scan the horizon

00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.919
for sight of them.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.921
They're 50 nautical miles away,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.891
then 20 miles before they turn away.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:05.592
I'm also,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.893
like I said a bit later,

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.128
to Russian warships

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:08.895
approach

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.529
coming within

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.698
just five miles of the task force.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.099
This force

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.034
like the alliance, is international

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.436
with ships from the German,

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.370
Portuguese,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.771
Spanish, Polish,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.274
Danish and French navies.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.343
I climb down the side of the Mecklenburg

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.110
for a fast

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.279
boat ride to the Portuguese frigate

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.847
Bartolomeo Diaz.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.150
They are members of

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:30.717
Portuguese

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.951
elite Special Forces

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.187
drill for an attack by small boats.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.656
Their guns trained on the horizon,

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.692
watching and waiting.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.293
Helicopters

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.595
patrol the waters day and night

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.466
These are exercises, but soldiers

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.234
and sailors make clear

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.103
they are training and readying

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.337
for the real thing.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.541
We have to be capable to switch

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.911
every hour from an anti-submarine mission

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.913
to an end to surface mission

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.849
to a passenger transport

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.818
deployment of Special Forces.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:06.352
So

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.888
every day is different.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.724
The war in Ukraine looms large here

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.692
This task force

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.426
now sails

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.794
with twice as many ships

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.563
and sailors as before the invasion.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.664
And as the task force

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.199
commander told me,

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.200
they are NATO's

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.634
first line of defense

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.136
against any new acts

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.238
of Russian aggression.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.674
We ended our trip in Estonia.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.308
And I'll tell you, Wolf,

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.442
when you go to the Eastern,

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.177
facing NATO's allies such as Estonia

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.612
and I met the prime minister

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.681
while I was there, I kind of colors.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.749
They speak in even starker terms

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.551
than the western side of the alliance.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.420
They see Russia as a continuing threat.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:40.887
In effect,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.022
they don't put anything past Putin.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.957
They're nervous

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.391
that he might attack the alliance

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.859
and they're preparing for it.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:47.860
Very disturbing indeed.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.628
Excellent reporting.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.396
Jim Sciutto, thank you very, very much.

